<p>Now more than ever, there’s tremendous pressure to make it big while you’re young.</p>
<p>Pity the 31-year-old who fails to make it onto a 30-under-30 list…</p>
<p>The soon-to-graduate high schooler passed over for YouTube stardom…</p>
<p>The great hordes who&nbsp;creep into middle age without so much as a TED Talk to their names…</p>
<p>Social media definitely magnifies the sensation that an unacceptable number of our peers have been granted first-class cabins aboard a ship that’s sailed without us. If we weren’t so demoralized, we’d sue Instagram for creating the impression that everyone else’s perfectly filtered life is leading to book deals and profiles in <em>The New Yorker</em>.</p>
